From b63470d46788aed9d4a4d0401435639caeb8f3e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:54:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Supabase auth, optional store branches and row-level
 security

- Supabase session resolver: verifies access tokens locally against the
  project's public keys (ES256/RS256 only), maps the user to a staff account
  through staff_users.auth_user_id, and requires aal2 (403 MFA_REQUIRED).
  Production now refuses to start without SUPABASE_URL.
- Optional store branches (store_locations): points stay per store, awards
  record their branch, members can be limited to one. The database enforces
  that a branch belongs to the same store.
- Row-level security enabled on every table, with a test that fails if a new
  table forgets it.
- bootstrap:admin and staff:login scripts; dev server reads .env.
- Fix: migration 0005 was not in the Drizzle journal, so drizzle-kit migrate
  would have skipped it. Replace it with a generated migration and add a test
  that keeps the journal and the files in step.
- Docs: D-098 to D-106, HANDOFF, STATUS, RUNBOOK, README.

45 unit and 111 integration tests pass.
